_score_sbc_dilution":86.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.0035899999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"BWX Technologies, Inc. manufactures and sells nuclear components in the United States, Canada, and internationally. The company operates through two segments, Government Operations and Commercial Operations. It manufactures precision naval nuclear components, reactors, and nuclear fuel; close-tolerance and high-quality equipment for nuclear applications; critical nuclear components, fuels and assemblies for government and limited other uses; down blend government stockpiles of uranium; and fabricate fuel-bearing precision components. The company also supplies proprietary and sole-source valves, manifolds, and fittings to naval and commercial shipping customers; research reactor fuel elements for colleges, universities, and national laboratories; and components for defense applications. In addition, it manufactures commercial nuclear steam generators, nuclear fuel, fuel handling systems, pressure vessels, reactor components, heat exchangers, tooling delivery systems; and containers for the storage of nuclear fuel and other high-level nuclear waste. Further, the company supplies nuclear fuel, fuel handling systems, tooling delivery systems, nuclear-grade materials and precisely machined components; and manufactures medical radioisotopes, radiopharmaceuticals, and medical devices. Additionally, it provides specialized engineering services that include structural component design, 3-D thermal-hydraulic engineering analysis, weld and robotic process development, electrical and controls engineering and metallurgy and materials engineering; in-plant inspection, maintenance and modification services; and non-destructive examination and tooling/repair solutions. It also offers nuclear power plant lifecycle support and management services. The company was formerly known as The Babcock & Wilcox Company and changed its name to BWX Technologies, Inc. in June 2015. BWX Technologies, Inc. was founded in 1867 and is headquartered in Lynchburg, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rex D. Geveden | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $308K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $28K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["BWX Technologies, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $9.9B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $295M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.46\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 9.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 85% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8485721708481406},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.8M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3773130.79},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 14% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Will BWX (NYSE:BWXT) Impress In Its Next Release?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/will-bwx-nysebwxt-impress-in-its-next-release","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795199340.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(BWXT) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutiona